[2026-09-26T16:00:16.968+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] # leaf-full-design
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.968+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.968+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] Use this skill when you determine the current node owns the smallest executable feature slice required by its scenarios.
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.968+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.968+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] ## Instructions
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.968+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.968+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 1. Treat the current node as owning the smallest executable feature slice required by its scenarios.
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.968+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 2. Design only interfaces needed for the owned chain, which may span UI -> API -> FUNC -> DB when those layers are truly owned by the leaf.
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.968+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 3. Prefer existing entrypoints, boundary files, services, and persistence scaffolds before creating new owners.
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.968+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 4. Reuse existing parent/dependency interfaces when the leaf should implement, extend, or call them; return the existing `interface_id` so the current node can be attached to the same contract.
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.968+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 5. If a parent-designed UI shell is the user-facing entry for the leaf, include that UI interface in the leaf's interface list and connect it to leaf-owned API/FUNC/DB interfaces through callers/callees.
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.968+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 6. Materialize only minimal compilable owner files or skeleton code during DESIGN when the interface would otherwise be only abstract JSON.
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.968+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 7. Do not implement full validation, persistence, authentication/session semantics, encryption, or business behavior in DESIGN; that belongs to TestDrivenDeveloper.
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.968+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 8. Avoid large file writes in DESIGN. Prefer route/client/service/database placeholders with explicit TODO-free contract shape over complete feature implementation.
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.968+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 9. Do not hardcode screenshot data, sample rows, fake success messages, or fallback arrays as completed behavior.
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.968+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 10. Return interfaces that make later test generation straightforward: include `file_path`, `first_line`, responsibility, specification, callers/callees, and test focus.
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.968+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 11. The interface `type` must be one of `UI`, `API`, `FUNC`, or `DB`.
