[2026-09-26T16:00:16.970+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.970+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] # auth-session-consistency
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.970+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.970+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] Use this skill when a leaf node owns authentication/session behavior.
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.970+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.970+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] ## Instructions
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.970+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.970+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 1. Treat authentication state as a cross-cutting system contract, not a page-local success message.
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.970+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 2. Apply this skill to executable leaf-node work. Non-leaf UI/composition nodes may expose auth entry points or shell slots, but they do not design API, FUNC, or DB session contracts.
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.970+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 3. Design or reuse connected interfaces for UI session state, auth API routes, service logic, and session persistence when those layers are relevant.
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.970+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 4. Prefer existing shell/header/provider/client/server/database boundaries before creating new owners.
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.970+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 5. A registration or login success should update global authenticated state and expose a durable session recovery path.
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.970+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 6. Provide a session-loading API or equivalent runtime boundary when the app needs to restore authenticated state after refresh/navigation.
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.970+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 7. Header, navigation, protected/public route behavior, and current-user display should consume the same global session state rather than duplicating local page state.
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.970+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 8. Tests should verify observable global state transitions: unauthenticated chrome before the action, authenticated chrome/current-user state after the action, and session recovery when required by the scenario.
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.970+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 9. Do not satisfy authenticated-state requirements with only a page-local success banner, fake user object, local fallback array, or hardcoded header text.
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.970+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 10. Keep cookies/tokens/session records consistent across UI client, API responses, service logic, and DB schema.
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.970+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 11. Preserve parent shell ownership: if the header/shell is parent-designed, return and use that reused UI interface with callers/callees linked to leaf-owned auth/session interfaces.
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.970+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 12. Inspect
[2026-09-26T16:00:16.970+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] ...[truncated]
