[2026-09-26T16:02:28.037+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "first_line": 1,
[2026-09-26T16:02:28.037+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "responsibility": "Global single source of truth for the authenticated user, shared by the registration page, the sign-in page, and any shell/header that displays the current username so post-registration state survives navigation and reload.",
[2026-09-26T16:02:28.037+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "specification": "Exports AuthSessionProvider({children}) and useAuthSession(): { user: AuthUser | null, status: 'loading'|'ready', setUser(user|null), refreshSession(): Promise<AuthUser|null> }. On mount the provider calls refreshSession, which loads GET /api/auth/session and stores the result, giving the durable session-recovery path required after refresh. Successful registration (and sign-in) must call setUser with the server user object; consumers must read this context rather than keeping page-local user state. useAuthSession throws outside the provider. Provider mounting in main.tsx around <App/> is TDD wiring. AuthUser = { id, username, email, emailVerified: boolean }.",
[2026-09-26T16:02:28.037+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "inputs": "Server session payload from GET /api/auth/session; user objects returned by register/login responses.",
[2026-09-26T16:02:28.037+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "outputs": "Context value consumed by shell, route guards, and auth pages; authenticated state persists across reloads via session reload.",
[2026-09-26T16:02:28.037+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]       "callers": [
[2026-09-26T16:02:28.037+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]         "frontend/src/main.tsx (provider mount, TDD wiring)",
[2026-09-26T16:02:28.037+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]         "REQ-1-1-1-UI-REGISTRATION-PAGE",
[2026-09-26T16:02:28.037+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]         "sign-in page",
[2026-09-26T16:02:28.037+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1]         "app shell / header current-user display"
